  "id": "COMPOUND:30135 - PROTEIN:6336",
  "verbalization": "Tenacissoside B appears to have a shared target of Prelamin-A/C, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including 5,11-Dihydroxy-3,3-dimethylpyrano[3,2-a]xanthen-12-one, 3-O-Methyl Droserone, and Taxinine NN-7. All of these compounds ultimately target Thrombopoietin, suggesting a potential pathway where Tenacissoside B may influence Thrombopoietin through the activation of Prelamin-A/C. The evidence indicates that Tenacissoside B could act as a modulator of the signaling cascade involving Prelamin-A/C, which is known to be involved in blood cell production and regulation. The presence of multiple compounds with similar targets to Prelamin-A/C suggests a possible functional overlap or a shared biological role in the pathway leading to Thrombopoietin activation. This integrated evidence supports the hypothesis that Tenacissoside B may exert its effects on Thrombopoietin through a mechanism involving Prelamin-A/C, potentially by modulating the expression or activity of this protein.",
